# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF line endings, whatever core.autocrlf
# says on the machine that clones this repository. The tool writes LF, and the committed
# samples are compared with its output byte for byte, so a checkout that turned them into
# CRLF would fail that comparison on a tree nobody had changed. The Task XML samples are
# UTF-16, which git reads as binary and leaves alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
